# Build context sent to the Fly builder on every deploy. Without this it was
# 155 MB across 7,241 files — almost entirely venv/ — uploaded every time.
#
# Note this never affected the IMAGE: the Dockerfile COPYs a named list of
# files, so nothing extra was ever baked in. It was purely upload cost per
# deploy.

# Named explicitly, ahead of the catch-all below, so the context walker can skip
# these subtrees wholesale instead of stat-ing every file inside them.
venv/
.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime state. On Fly this lives on the mounted volume at /app/data; a local
# copy must never be baked into the image, where it would shadow the mount if
# the volume ever failed to attach.
data/

# Secrets. Telegram credentials come from `fly secrets`, never from the image.
.env

# Everything else is excluded too, and the list below re-includes exactly what
# the Dockerfile COPYs. An allowlist rather than a denylist because the
# Dockerfile is already one: the two stay in step, and a file added to the repo
# can't quietly start riding along in the context.
#
# If you add a COPY to the Dockerfile, add it here as well — otherwise the build
# fails with "file not found", which is the right way round to get that wrong.
*
!requirements.txt
!api.py
!debug.py
!defaults.py
!kline_volume.py
!dashboard.html
!favicon.ico
!start.sh
